What this covers
----------------

CC BY 4.0 applies to the solid-schema contents:

  - <Name>/index.json          — each type's JSON Schema 2020-12 file
  - schema/meta.schema.json    — meta-schema enforcing registry conventions
  - corpus.jsonl               — generated: every schema as one record per line
  - index.json                 — generated: name → schema URL
  - reverse-index.json         — generated: urn:solid type → schema URL

What this does NOT cover
------------------------

Build scripts remain licensed under AGPL-3.0 (see LICENSE):

  - scripts/*.js
  - generated <Name>/index.html, top-level index.html

Why
---

JSON Schemas are contracts — designed to be embedded in any product
that validates data. CC BY 4.0 means a JSON Schema for urn:solid:Person
can be dropped into a proprietary system with attribution but without
inheriting copyleft on the surrounding code.
